  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What the types guarantee",
      "items": [
        "Every MoveToTrash target passed PolicyEvaluator's cache rule and an ApprovalValidity consistency check. Evidence and approval are values the caller supplies, not proofs.",
        "EligibleCandidate.init and ReviewPlanTarget.init(candidate:) are internal, so a target cannot skip evaluateCache (15 min observed inactivity, named cache scope). GeneralMacFinding, Finding and FileObservation have public inits, so the evidence PolicyEvaluator.evaluate reads is caller-built.",
        "ReviewPlan has a private init; build(draft:digesting:) is the only way to get one, and it carries canonical bytes and the digest from the supplied PlanDigesting (the app uses SHA-256 via CryptoKitPlanDigestAdapter).",
        "MoveToTrash.init(target:) is internal; ApprovedTrashOperationFactory makes one only after ApprovalValidity returns .validForReview. ApprovalAttestation and ApprovalContext have public inits, and the app sets displayedDigest: plan.digest, currentTargets: plan.targets and approvedAt: now itself, so only the approved-digest and expiry checks can fail there.",
        "FreshTargetEvidence has a public memberwise init and observing(target:in:) takes raw findings; only observing(target:eligibleIn:), which the app uses, limits evidence to still-eligible findings.",
        "With the default probe, FoundationTrashAdapter re-validates fresh evidence, then re-probes inode, size, mtime, link count 1 and symlinks before its single trashItem(at:) call. Its public init accepts replacement identityProbe and nativeTrash closures and a caller-injected resolveRoot, and the re-probe does not re-check alias, package, mount, scope or inactivity. The app resolves only ~/Library/Caches and gives no fresh evidence outside com.apple.iconservices.store; a small check/use race remains."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Reading the notation",
      "items": [
        "Visibility: + public, ~ Swift internal (module only), - private.",
        "Each sublabel starts with the Swift kind. The letter badge repeats the diagram kind: C class, I interface, E enumeration, R record. «record» marks a value-type data struct; a plain header is a behaviour type (struct or actor); «interface» is a Swift protocol; «enumeration» is a Swift enum whose rows are its cases.",
        "A return written throws -> T or async -> T carries the Swift effect; an init marked : throws can fail.",
        "CryptoKitPlanDigestAdapter, FoundationTrashAdapter, FoundationReceiptExecutionAdapter and AppSupportReceiptStore are in CleanerCoreFoundation; the rest are in CleanerCore."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "References shown in members, not lines",
      "items": [
        "ReviewPlan.build takes a PlanDigesting; ReviewPlan also stores the targets.",
        "ApprovalValidity.evaluate takes the ReviewPlan; ApprovalContext.currentTargets and MoveToTrash.target hold ReviewPlanTarget.",
        "ReceiptHistoryCoordinator.run(intent:) has the store persist the ReceiptIntent before the first move. ReceiptIntent.planDigest records the caller-supplied plan digest; run() does not verify it.",
        "ReceiptExecutionConsuming returns TrashItemOutcome<PrivateRecoveryDestination>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Left out",
      "items": [
        "DisplayedPlanFactory.makePlan, which the app calls to rank eligible candidates into a ReviewPlanDraft and ReviewPlan.build.",
        "TrashExecutionCoordinator and TrashRunResult (both internal init) and ScriptedTrashExecutionPort, a test double shipped in CleanerCore: the app drives moves through ReceiptHistoryCoordinator instead.",
        "ReceiptLeasePort, ReceiptClock and receipt reconciliation, retention and reduction types."
      ]
    }
  ]
